  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to the organisation of the World Social Forum 2009</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The World Social Forum, a civil society initiative, is a democratic gathering that seeks to foster debates and the deepening of collective reflections, formulation of alternative proposals, exchange of experiences and the building of coalitions and networks among social movements, community-based organisations (CBOs), non-governmental organisations (NGOs) and other civil society organisations (CSOs) that oppose neo-liberalism and the injustices it creates.

From January 27th to February 2nd 2009 the 9th edition of othe WSF will take place in the Amazon Region in Northern Brazil.  The event will highlight the regions&apos;s environmental issues amidst an environmentally and socially unsustainable and hegemonic development model.  

The WSF has become the main reference to debate social and economic responsibility for our planet and our future.  It has united innumerable participants, activists, and leaders from social and popular movements, networks and campaigns, students, intellectuals, scientists, artists, journalists and other opinion makers.</narrative>
  </description>
